notes='Author page2, archive foot364. The title names Dold Puppe and Ann Inst Fourier. The page writes a derived symmetric-power expression, then defines two rows involving ZM_* and Sym M_*, with a vertical pair of wavy strokes. The internal stroke after Sym remains a parenthesis or slash; the final outer parenthesis is present. The first L subscript remains i or a star. A right margin attributes a weight grading to these expressions. The Dold Thom paragraph includes a dot as the first symmetric-product component, an ordinary arrow out of X_bullet and a circle around only pi_i SYM^infty X. The inserted English-form axioms replaces a short crossed fragment; no d-apostrophe precedes Eilenberg. The isolated group has exponent ell, not k. The Moore-space expressions and homology calculation use the same flattened K forms as the preceding pages. The lower L_i Sym(G) has no n in its argument, despite the n in the surrounding expressions; none is supplied. The relation under the ZM underbrace remains doubtful. A cancelled right-margin diagram preserves its arrows and the legible Ext(G,H), but retains doubt over its second source and the final argument of Hom. The Dold comparison points left from Sym ZX, with ZX underlined. The bottom comparison raises both n and the homology index by1, leaving the relative index r unchanged; this is an indexing check only. The only live range written is r<n, with n<=r<=2n deleted. No lower bound on r or reduced-homology convention is stated here, and no stability theorem is proved or imported to fill that omission. No date or source heading follows the archive number; H’s final editorial heading is not manuscript text.'
